 to have too much  extra puff pastry  cause it'll just be like too bready and  also it might not cook like all the way  through if there's a lot of extra kind  of bunched up right there so classically  in a wellington the puff pastry is  brushed with english mustard you could  really use any like mustard variety that  you like like a dijon or just a regular  yellow mustard but english mustard has a  ton of flavor and a really bright  vibrant yellow color and you can usually  find it at most grocery stores so once  your chickens are cooled and set pop  that right on the puff pastry and give  it a wrap now again if you have too much  extra puff pastry trim that off and then  you can tuck the sides under and kind of  fix it so it looks really nice the egg  wash will help your puff pastry get  really nice and brown and golden color  once it's baked so then it's time to get  a little fancy with it so in order to  create a nice design on the outside i  took a fork and kind of drew marks in  the puff pastry itself so i did the  lines one way and then i went back and  did it diagonally so it had a nice kind  of diamond pattern on the puff pastry so  once it bakes it looks really nice and  pretty then hit it with a little more  salt  and you're ready to bake salt bae that  ish  so you want to bake your rolls until of  course the chicken is cooked through now  this chicken will actually cook pretty  fast because it's pounded out so thin so  it just won't take as long to cook as  like a full piece of chicken breast  but you also are looking for a really  deep golden brown color on the puff  pastry to make sure it's all the way  cooked through  pounding out the chicken breasts and  rolling it up like this will help you  get that really beautiful spiral center  that every chicken cordon bleu should  have also what's great about using the  puff pastry as opposed to a classic  chicken cordon bleu breading is that  it's so much cleaner breading is often  pretty messy since you have like a lot  going on with the egg and the bread  crumbs and the flour  but this you get it all in one go and  no mess no fuss  it's what i like  this dish is also super show-stopping  it's a great dish for a dinner party  they're pretty big so you might not need  to eat the whole thing but they look  really fancy and they taste even better  hello my name is alvin and today i will  be showing you my recipe for chicken  parmesan stuffed garlic bread  [Music]  so this is definitely one of my more  crazier tasty recipes i sat on this  concept for like six months i'm not even  kidding i really want to combine garlic  bread with something else because  everybody likes garlic bread and garlic  bread should not be only a side dish it  deserves to be the main attraction i  want to combine it with something that's  like an entree so i was like oh what do  you eat garlic bread with uh meatballs  spaghetti pasta chicken parm oh chicken  parm sounds really good it's got  everything that garlic bread needs in a  best friend i was like i need to find a  way to make chicken parmesan mixed in  with garlic bread so my idea was that  instead of doing a whole chicken breast  i would cut chicken breast up into  smaller strips bread them fry them  separately so you almost have like these  little chicken tenders that you can work  with  [Music]  after that i would wrap each chicken  tender with a slice of mozzarella cheese  because that's what chicken farm needs  and then i would take this little like  chicken cheese cylindrical thingy and  put it inside a hollowed out baguette i  think that you need to make sure that  you get a baguette that is not too thin  because you're going to hollow it out  because you're going to hollow out the  baguette you need to make sure that you  take a really thin sharp knife and cut  out like the filling of the bread we  don't want to waste that you can use  that for croutons you know sometimes the  middle of the bread can be the best part  i ate way too 